require --trigger for hybrid; clearer drain-miss error; redesign andesim --help

The hybrid composition no longer guesses the ROI delimiter, the cryptic
drain-mismatch error explains itself, every required flag hints when missing,
and `andesim --help` is a readable command tree.

- hybrid_trigger: --trigger marker|pc is now REQUIRED (no silent marker
  default). Empty -> "--trigger marker|pc is required (the ROI delimiter; see
  'andesim run --help')".
- run_plan: a drain leg that exits 0 ran the workload to completion without
  reaching its ROI boundary -- the trigger never fired. Say exactly that
  (naming the leg role + trigger kind) instead of "expected exit 200, got 0".
  Extracted as plan_step_rc_error; the drain code is now named kDrainRc.
- required-flag hints: filled the bare "missing ELF" (now names the workload)
  and added a `--help` pointer to the --mode / --trigger errors.
- main.cpp: --help redesigned into a tree -- run/list as major commands with
  their subcommands (modes / targets) and run's full option list, REQUIRED
  flags marked; dev options + the fixtures target behind ANDESIM_DEV. run
  --help / list --help slice the same one model. Dropped the now-dead Tier
  field and folded the option indent into the flag literal.

Behavioral (trigger requirement, error text, help layout) + structural (help
model, plan_step_rc_error extraction, Tier/indent cleanup). TDD: RED tests
first in hybrid_test, plan_test, f7, f9, release_surface. Contract suite green
(release_surface/f7/f9/cosim/verify/cosim_refine/cosim_lockstep/trigger_gating/
memsize); cosim.sh's --cosim-interval-0 case gains --trigger marker since the
required check now precedes it.

